// EYENET - host Docker daemon defaults. Copy to /etc/docker/daemon.json on the
// prod host and `systemctl restart docker`. This caps EVERY container's json-file
// logs host-wide (postgres, nats, loki, the collector itself, and anything added
// later), so the per-service `logging:` anchor in compose.yaml becomes a belt on
// top of these suspenders. Host-level, like fail2ban and the EDR exclusion.
{
  "log-driver": "json-file",
  "log-opts": {
    "max-size": "20m",
    "max-file": "5"
  }
}
